From platform#275 (cai-platform). The usage contract (cai-gpm docs/vertrag/nutzung.md, section node_kind) lists four per-request fields; the usage event already carries finish_reason, ttft_ms and correlation_id (k121), but not node_kind.

Wanted: node_kind on every usage event that has a node:
- gpm: the node came from the GPM node list (id starts with gpm-), also static engines the GPM publishes;
- forward: forwarded to another Skeid (node_id starts with org-skeid-);
- static: the node is configured directly in Skeid;
- absent: no node (request dropped before routing).
node_kind and the id prefix must agree.

The platform reads it tolerantly (unknown value = empty) and will then count forwarded rows and ttft_ms by node_kind instead of the prefix.
